From 822569010ce34a6c58539509f482ced7b0c4d428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:57:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ucm2: MediaTek: add mt8901-soundwir for MT8901 SoundWire
 laptops

Add UCM profiles for the MediaTek MT8901 SoundWire audio card as
found in the NVIDIA RTX Spark laptops. The card driver is
"mt8901-soundwir". The card exposes no component string, so the
dispatcher identifies the board by which SoundWire peripherals
enumerated, through the sysfs device names the SoundWire core
creates under /sys/bus/soundwire/devices, and selects a per-topology
profile. Six variants are covered:

 - 4x CS35L56 on link 0, CS42L43 on link 1
 - 2x RT1321 on link 0, RT713 on link 1
 - CS42L43 and 2x CS35L56, all on link 1
 - CS42L43 and 4x CS35L56, all on link 1
 - 2x RT1320 on link 0, RT712 on link 1 (two board variants,
   distinguished by the amplifier unique ids)

Each profile provides Speaker, Headphones, Headset microphone and
internal microphone devices on the HiFi verb with the interconnect
routes for that topology, and puts a default capture route in the verb
so the capture PCM opens at profile probe time.

Signed-off-by: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
