From 7d3555a754936ce073ce5fe3d623294d81dd5c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:42:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ucm2: MediaTek: mt8901-soundwir: make the Cirrus profile
 conditions exclusive

The three Cirrus topologies were matched by independent If blocks keyed on
one SoundWire peripheral each. A board that carries the CS42L43 on link 1
together with four CS35L56 on link 0 satisfies both the cs35l56x4_cs42l43
condition and the cs42l43_cs35l56x2 one (the CS42L43 on link 1 exists on
both), and a board with four CS35L56 on link 1 satisfies cs42l43_cs35l56x4
and cs42l43_cs35l56x2. Two HiFi verb definitions were then included and
which one applied was up to the parser.

Nest the link 1 checks under the False branch of the preceding block so
exactly one profile is selected: four CS35L56 on link 0 first, then four
on link 1, then the two amplifier layout.

Reported-by: Andreas Glinserer <andreas.glinserer@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit e77bb29251752384c54bb51c32b7e6ca853334d1)
---
 .../mt8901-soundwir/mt8901-soundwir.conf      | 58 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

